# Milestone: M3
# Covers: loader rejects v1.1 (M2) bytecode modules at v1.2 runtime
#
# blocked: needs a `## host:` body.  The host driver has existed since
# the core re-foundation (tests/integration/chk_host_driver.c) -- what is
# missing is this fixture, rewritten to drive its own clock and its own
# urbi_step calls.  That is per-fixture authoring work, scheduled with the
# rest of the corpus in Phase 5.  The annotation it replaced said the
# driver did not exist, which stopped being true at Task 12.
# matrix-row: wire-format
#
# Reason: the chk runner (tests/integration/run_chk.sh) feeds .u source text
# into the REPL.  There is no mechanism to inject a pre-baked binary blob and
# call uchunk_deserialize directly.  The runtime behaviour being tested here
# (UCHUNK_LOAD_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION for version byte 0x11) is already covered by the
# C unit tests:
#   - "deserialize rejects v1.1 module (M2 hard break)"  in tests/unit/test_module.c
#   - "deserialize rejects v1.0 module"                  in tests/unit/test_module.c
#
# When T44 (M3 legacy chk corpus port) adds binary-blob injection support to
# the runner, implement this fixture by:
#   1. Emitting a minimal module at v1.1 format using the M2 emitter (or hand-
#      crafting a 30-byte blob with version byte 0x11 at offset 4).
#   2. Loading it via the T44-era --load-bytecode flag (or equivalent) and
#      asserting the output contains "unsupported version byte 0x11".
